[h1]Occupation & Annexation[/h1]

Enemy settlements no longer have to be wiped out. Break their defense and the survivors [b]capitulate[/b]: they drop their weapons and lie face down. Occupy the town, win its loyalty, [b]annex[/b] it into your Protectorate, collect what it produces and visit it.

[h2]Capitulation[/h2]
[list]
[*]While you assault a settlement, the defenders' morale is tracked: lost fighters, destroyed turrets, a fallen commander, suppression (Combat Extended) and being outnumbered. When it breaks, every survivor surrenders.
[*]Those who surrendered are no threat: colonists and turrets ignore them. Right-click one to [b]take them prisoner[/b] on the spot.
[*]Settlement defenders no longer flee off the map; they hold out until they give up (configurable).
[*]Once the shooting stops for 15–40 seconds, their medics get up: they stop the bleeding, [b]carry the downed into the town's beds[/b] and tend the wounded. Fire at them and everyone lies face down again.
[*]Fire comes first, ceasefire or not: whoever catches fire rolls it out, and the nearest one on their feet puts out a comrade burning on the ground. Burns from a fire you lit earlier are not a new attack.
[*][b]Your doctors can tend them too[/b], drafted or not. The town will remember it.
[*]Killing someone who surrendered upsets your colonists according to their ideoligion (or their traits) and costs goodwill with other factions. Spare them all and your people feel better for it.
[/list]

[h2]Occupied towns[/h2]
[list]
[*]Instead of ruins, the settlement becomes a town of your [b]Protectorate[/b], a permanently allied faction. Its buildings and turrets switch sides.
[*][b]Loyalty[/b] grows over time, faster with a garrison, low taxes and gifts. Annex the town once it is ready.
[*][b]Economy[/b]: towns produce goods from their workshops and fields; taxes bring silver. Build more workshops during a visit to change what a town makes. Production profiles are XML and can be extended by other mods.
[*]Take goods by caravan, or request a [b]delivery[/b] by pack animals or drop pods.
[*][b]Visits[/b]: a town is rebuilt as you left it, and the locals work, farm, haul, repair battle damage, patrol, socialise and sleep on a daily routine.
[*][b]Population[/b]: loyal towns attract newcomers until their beds are full; annexed towns send volunteers to your colony.
[*][b]Militia[/b]: townsfolk take weapons from the stockpile to fight off the former owners.
[*][b]Events[/b]: disloyal towns may rise up, and former owners may try to retake their town, with two days of warning.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements and compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld 1.5. Tested with all four DLCs.
[*]Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url].
[*]Optional support for [b]Combat Extended[/b] (suppression lowers morale; the surrendered ignore it and don't re-arm) and [b]CAI 5000[/b] (its combat AI leaves the surrendered alone).
[*]Vehicle Framework caravans can be reformed in occupied towns, and Real Ruins stays out of town maps.
[*]Safe to add to an existing save. [b]Not safe to remove[/b] from a save that has occupied towns.
[*]English and Ukrainian.
[/list]

Everything can be tuned in the mod settings.

[h2]Notes[/h2]
This mod was created using an LLM, so please keep that in mind if you use it.

Bug reports and source code: [url=https://github.com/Devlonic/Occupation---Annexation]GitHub[/url]. Please attach your Player.log (%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Ludeon Studios\RimWorld by Ludeon Studios).
